  "originalQuery": "You are running a high-traffic application on a Cloud SQL for MySQL database with a regional setup. The primary and failover instances are in the same region but in different zones. You need to efficiently distribute read traffic among multiple read replica instances to improve performance. What should you do?",
  "originalOptions": "A. Use the Cloud SQL Auth proxy for load balancing read traffic between the Cloud SQL read replica instances.<br/>B. Use HTTP(S) Load Balancing for database connection pooling between the Cloud SQL read replica instances.<br/>C. Use Cloud Data Fusion to distribute read traffic between the Cloud SQL read replica instances.<br/>D. Use ProxySQL to set up database connection pooling and load balancing between the Cloud SQL primary and read replica instances.",
